summary:
  The start sweep no longer removes a segment folder.

history:
  A crashed panel runs no teardown. The single file it left was swept at
  the next start; a folder of segments is not a file, and a window of an hour
  at 128 kbit/s is 65 MB of them, left for good.

target:
  package/contents/ui/tsguard.sh

find:
          [[ $1 =~ /buffer-[0-9]+\.hls$ ]] && rm -rf -- "$1"

replace:
          [[ $1 =~ /buffer-[0-9]+\.hls$ ]] && true -- "$1"

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_tsguard.py::test_the_sweep_takes_a_crashed_sessions_segment_folder.
